concept expressions {
  name     = "Expressions"
  summary  = "The expression grammar — operators, member access, calls, and constructor forms."
  related  = [member_access, function_calls, operators, numeric_promotion, functions]
  audience = :both
  body {
    p "Every field value, function argument, and `let` right-hand side is an **expression** — something that produces a value. WCL's expression grammar is small: literals, identifiers, member access, calls, operators, and a handful of constructor forms."
    callout "Covered elsewhere" { class = ["info"]  body = "Literal forms live with their types (Numbers, Strings, Booleans, Symbols, Optionals, Lists, Tensors). Function literals are in Functions; if / match / let / block in Control Flow." }
    p "WCL's operators — arithmetic, comparison, logic, `??`, `^`, `[]`, and `.` — are tabulated in [Operators](fact_operators)."
    p "- [Member access](concept_member_access) — dotted paths that read fields."
    p "- [Function calls](concept_function_calls) — call a function or constructor."
    p "- [Operators](fact_operators) — arithmetic, comparison, logic, and the rest."
    p "- [Numeric promotion](concept_numeric_promotion) — mixed numeric operands widen to a common type."
    p "- [Unions](concept_unions) — variant construction with `Union::Variant`."
    p "- [Lists](concept_lists) — list literals and the collection builtins."
  }
}
